### Demo requests (IntelliJ HTTP client / VS Code REST Client).
### Each order's status settles a moment after it's placed. Poll GET /orders/{id}.

### Catalog
GET http://localhost:8082/products

### 1. Happy path: total under 1000 → CONFIRMED
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "ana@example.com",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "KEYBOARD", "quantity": 1 },
    { "sku": "MOUSE", "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}

### 2. Out of stock (only 3 monitors) → CANCELLED, stock unchanged
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "bob@example.com",
  "items": [ { "sku": "MONITOR", "quantity": 5 } ]
}

### 3. Payment declined (total above 1000) → CANCELLED, stock released
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "carol@example.com",
  "items": [ { "sku": "LAPTOP", "quantity": 1 } ]
}

### 4. Unknown product → 400, rejected synchronously
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "dan@example.com",
  "items": [ { "sku": "NOPE", "quantity": 1 } ]
}

### 5. Invalid request → 400 (Spring's default ProblemDetail, TODO(error-handler))
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerEmail": "not-an-email", "items": [] }

### 6. Idempotency flaw: send this twice → two orders. TODO(idempotency)
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-Idempotency-Key: demo-key-1

{
  "customerEmail": "erin@example.com",
  "items": [ { "sku": "MOUSE", "quantity": 1 } ]
}

### Orders
GET http://localhost:8081/orders

### Payments
GET http://localhost:8083/payments
